# Trivy ignore list — accepted CVEs in Debian 13 (bookworm) base image.
#
# These CVEs are flagged HIGH but are accepted as known issues until Debian
# ships a fix. Each entry must include rationale.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-06-10
# Re-check periodically: `trivy image --severity HIGH ghcr.io/cerez23/nimbusguard/backend:latest`
# When a fix is available in Debian, remove the entry and rebuild the image.
#

# CVE-2025-69720 — ncurses buffer overflow.
# Affected: libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin (no Debian fix yet).
# Rationale: exploit requires attacker-controlled input fed to an ncurses-based
# CLI tool. The backend container does not run any interactive terminal program
# and does not expose ncurses to network input. Risk in our deployment: minimal.
CVE-2025-69720

# CVE-2026-29111 — systemd arbitrary code execution / DoS via spurious IPC.
# Affected: libsystemd0, libudev1 (no Debian fix yet).
# Rationale: requires local IPC access to a running systemd instance. The
# container does NOT run systemd as PID 1 (uvicorn is the entrypoint), so the
# attack surface does not exist in our deployment. The libs are pulled in only
# as transitive dependencies and never invoked.
CVE-2026-29111

# perl-base CVEs (CRITICAL/HIGH) — Debian 13 (trixie), status fix_deferred /
# affected (no Debian fix available; `apt-get upgrade` cannot resolve them).
# Affected: perl-base 5.40.1-6, an Essential Debian package that cannot be
# removed without breaking dpkg/apt.
# Rationale: the backend is a Python/uvicorn service. It runs NO Perl scripts
# and never invokes the vulnerable modules (Archive::Tar, IO::Compress,
# IO::Uncompress::Unzip) or the Perl compiler. Every one of these CVEs requires
# attacker-controlled input to be fed to a Perl archive/compress tool, which
# does not happen in our deployment — perl-base is present only as a transitive
# base-image dependency. Re-check when Debian publishes a fixed perl-base.
# CVE-2026-42496 — perl-archive-tar: path traversal via crafted symlinks (CRITICAL)
CVE-2026-42496
# CVE-2026-8376 — perl: heap buffer overflow compiling crafted regex (CRITICAL)
CVE-2026-8376
# CVE-2026-42497 — Archive::Tar < 3.08: hardlink extraction attack
CVE-2026-42497
# CVE-2026-48959 — IO::Uncompress::Unzip < 2.220: CPU exhaustion
CVE-2026-48959
# CVE-2026-48962 — perl-IO-Compress: ACE via attacker-controlled output glob
CVE-2026-48962
# CVE-2026-9538 — Archive::Tar < 3.10: memory exhaustion
CVE-2026-9538
